* `-N <job name>` &mdash; Declares a custom name for the job. If not specified, 
  the job name will be the base name of the job script file.

* `-l walltime=<walltime>` &mdash; How much real-world time (walltime)
  will your job take to run? Must be an string in the following format:
  `HH:MM:SS`, `MM:SS`, or `SS.

* `-l ncpus=<ncpus>` &mdash; How many CPUs does your job need? If you only need
  one CPU you can leave this out.

* `-l mem=<bytes>` &mdash; How much memory does your job need? Must be
  an integer followed by M, G, or T to specify Mega, Giga or Terabytes.